WEBVTT

00:23:27.392 --> 00:23:30.325
And the upside is that problems
are really complex,

00:23:30.349 --> 00:23:32.802
and you want a leader
who's thinking things through

00:23:32.826 --> 00:23:34.584
and not just behaving rashly.

00:23:34.608 --> 00:23:38.557
If you want the extroverted counterpart,
there's Steve Ballmer,

00:23:38.581 --> 00:23:41.036
who was kind of the counterpart to that.

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:45.479
And I think that most people
who have more extreme temperaments

00:23:45.503 --> 00:23:47.119
in one direction or another,

00:23:47.143 --> 00:23:49.736
if they're self-aware enough
to be good leaders,

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:51.703
they usually know that about themselves,

00:23:51.727 --> 00:23:54.952
and they look for people around them
who will complement them,

00:23:54.976 --> 00:23:57.852
which makes everybody
happier and more effective.

00:23:57.876 --> 00:24:00.596
CA: I mean, Bill Gates probably
benefited for a long time